(PREFACE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IF the ways and slang of Vagabonds and Beggars interested Martin Luther) Tj T*
(enough to make him write a preface to the _Liber Vagatorum_[1] in 1528,) Tj T*
(two of the ungodly may be excused for caring, in 1869, for the old) Tj T*
(Rogues of their English land, and for putting together three of the) Tj T*
(earliest tracts about them. Moreover, these tracts are part of the) Tj T*
(illustrative matter that we want round our great book on Elizabethan) Tj T*
(England, Harrison's _Description of Britain_, and the chief of them is) Tj T*
(quoted by the excellent parson who wrote that book.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The first of these three tracts, Awdeley's _Fraternitye of Vacabondes_,) Tj T*
(has been treated by many hasty bibliographers, who can never have taken) Tj T*
(the trouble to read the first three leaves of Harman's book, as later) Tj T*
(than, and a mere pilfering from, Harman's _Caueat_. No such accusation,) Tj T*
(however, did Harman himself bring against the worthy printer-author) Tj T*
(\(herein like printer-author Crowley, though he was preacher too,\) who) Tj T*
(preceded him. In his Epistle dedicatory to the Countes of Shrewsbury, p.) Tj T*
(20, below, Harman, after speaking of 'these wyly wanderers,' vagabonds,) Tj T*
(says in 1566 or 1567,) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    There was _a fewe yeares since_ a small bréefe setforth of some) Tj T*
(    zelous man to his countrey,--of whom I knowe not,--that made a lytle) Tj T*
(    shewe of there names and vsage, and gaue a glymsinge lyghte, not) Tj T*
(    sufficient to perswade of their peuishe peltinge and pickinge) Tj T*
(    practyses, but well worthy of prayse.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Header: AWDELEY'S _FRATERNITYE OF VACABONDES_.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This description of the 'small bréefe,' and the 'lytle shewe' of the) Tj T*
('names and vsage,' exactly suits Awdeley's tract; and the 'fewe yeares) Tj T*
(since' also suits the date of what may be safely assumed to be the first) Tj T*
(edition of the _Fraternitye_, by John Awdeley or John Sampson, or) Tj T*
