(description or eulogy here. It is _the_ standard work on its) Tj T*
(subject,--'these rowsey, ragged, rabblement of rakehelles' \(p. 19\)--and) Tj T*
(has been largely plundered by divers literary cadgers. No copy of the) Tj T*
(first edition seems to be known to bibliographers. It was published in) Tj T*
(1566 or 1567,--probably the latter year,[4]--and must \(I conclude\) have) Tj T*
(contained less than the second, as in that's 'Harman to the Reader,' p.) Tj T*
(28, below, he says 'well good reader, I meane not to be tedyous vnto) Tj T*
(the, but haue added fyue or sixe more tales, because some of them weare) Tj T*
(doune whyle my booke was fyrste in the presse.' He speaks again of his) Tj T*
(first edition at p. 44, below, 'I had the best geldinge stolen oute of) Tj T*
(my pasture, that I had amongst others, whyle this boke was _first a) Tj T*
(printynge_;' and also at p. 51, below, 'Apon Alhollenday in the morning) Tj T*
(last anno domini 1566, or my booke was halfe printed, I meane _the first) Tj T*
(impression_.' All Hallows' or All Saints' Day is November 1.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Header: HARMAN'S _CAUEAT_: THE TWO STATES OF THE 2ND EDITION.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The edition called the second[5], also bearing date in 1567, is known to) Tj T*
(us in two states, the latter of which I have called the third edition.) Tj T*
(The first state of the second edition is shown by the Bodleian copy,) Tj T*
(which is 'Augmented and inlarged by the fyrst author here of,' and has,) Tj T*
(besides smaller differences specified in the footnotes in our pages,) Tj T*
(this great difference, that the arrangement of 'The Names of the) Tj T*
(Vpright Men, Roges, and Pallyards' is not alphabetical, by the first) Tj T*
(letter of the Christian names, as in the second state of the second) Tj T*
