(    ordeineth this maner of correction. The roge being apprehended,) Tj T*
(    committed to prison, and tried in the next assises \(whether they be) Tj T*
(    of gaole deliuerie or sessions of the peace\) if he happen to be) Tj T*
(    conuicted for a vagabond either by inquest of office, or the) Tj T*
(    testimonie of two honest and credible witnesses vpon their oths, he) Tj T*
(    is then immediatlie adiudged to be greeuouslie whipped and burned) Tj T*
(    through the gristle of the right eare, with an hot iron of the) Tj T*
(    compasse of an inch about, as a manifestation of his wicked life,) Tj T*
(    and due punishment receiued for the same. And this iudgement is to) Tj T*
(    be executed vpon him, except some honest person woorth fiue pounds) Tj T*
(    in the queene's books in goods, or twentie shillings in lands, or) Tj T*
(    some rich housholder to be allowed by the iustices, will be bound in) Tj T*
(    recognisance to reteine him in his seruice for one whole yeare. If) Tj T*
(    he be taken the second time, and proued to haue forsaken his said) Tj T*
(    seruice, he shall then be whipped againe, bored likewise through the) Tj T*
(    other eare and set to seruice: from whence if he depart before a) Tj T*
(    yeare be expired, and happen afterward to be attached againe, he is) Tj T*
(    condemned to suffer paines of death as a fellon \(except before) Tj T*
(    excepted\) without benefit of clergie or sanctuarie, as by the) Tj T*
(    statute dooth appeare. Among roges and idle persons finallie, we) Tj T*
(    find to be comprised all proctors that go vp and downe with) Tj T*
(    counterfeit licences, coosiners, and such as gad about the countrie,) Tj T*
(    vsing vnlawfull games, practisers of physiognomie, and palmestrie,) Tj T*
(    tellers of fortunes, fensers, plaiers,[30] minstrels, iugglers,) Tj T*
