(After a short description of the four ages of the world, there is an) Tj T*
(account of a feast, at which were present all kinds of vagabonds. Dekker) Tj T*
(was conveyed, by 'an old nimble-tong'd beldam, who seemed to haue the) Tj T*
(command of the place,' to an upper loft, 'where, vnseene, I might,) Tj T*
(through a wooden Latice that had prospect of the dining roome, both see) Tj T*
(and heare all that was to be done or spoken.') Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    'The whole assembly being thus gathered together, one, amongest the) Tj T*
(    rest, who tooke vpon him a Seniority ouer the rest, charged euery) Tj T*
(    man to answer to his name, to see if the Iury were full:--the Bill) Tj T*
(    by which hee meant to call them beeing a double Iug of ale \(that had) Tj T*
(    the spirit of _Aquavitæ_ in it, it smelt so strong\), and that hee) Tj T*
(    held in his hand. Another, standing by, with a toast, nutmeg, and) Tj T*
(    ginger, ready to cry _Vous avez_ as they were cald, and all that) Tj T*
(    were in the roome hauing single pots by the eares, which, like) Tj T*
(    Pistols, were charged to goe off so soone as euer they heard their) Tj T*
(    names. This Ceremony beeing set abroach, an Oyes was made. But he) Tj T*
(    that was Rector Chory \(the Captain of the Tatterdemalions\) spying) Tj T*
(    one to march vnder his Colours, that had neuer before serued in) Tj T*
(    those lowsie warres, paused awhile \(after hee had taken his first) Tj T*
(    draught, to tast the dexterity of the liquor\), and then began,) Tj T*
(    Iustice-like, to examine this yonger brother vpon interrogatories.') Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This yonger brother is afterwards 'stalled to the rogue;' and the) Tj T*
('Rector Chory[34]' instructs him in his duties, and tells him the names) Tj T*
