(The growth of the present Text was on this wise: Mr Viles suggested a) Tj T*
(reprint of Stace's reprint of Harman in 1573, after it had been read) Tj T*
(with the original, and collated with the earlier editions. The first) Tj T*
(edition I could not find, but ascertained, with some trouble, and) Tj T*
(through Mr W. C. Hazlitt, where the second and third editions were, and) Tj T*
(borrowed the 3rd of its ever-generous owner, Mr Henry Huth. Then Mr) Tj T*
(Hazlitt told me of Awdeley, which he thought was borrowed from Harman.) Tj T*
(However, Harman's own words soon settled that point; and Awdeley had to) Tj T*
(precede Harman. Then the real bagger from Harman, the _Groundworke_, had) Tj T*
(to be added, after the Parson's Sermon. Mr Viles read the proofs and) Tj T*
(revises of Harman with the original: Mr Wood and I have made the Index;) Tj T*
(and I, because Mr Viles is more desperately busy than myself, have) Tj T*
(written the Preface.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Header: MR PAYNE COLLIER'S WORK AND ALTERATIONS.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The extracts from Mr J. P. Collier must be taken for what they are) Tj T*
(worth. I have not had time to verify them; but assume them to be) Tj T*
(correct, and not ingeniously or unreasonably altered from their) Tj T*
(originals, like Mr Collier's print of Henslowe's Memorial, of which Dr) Tj T*
(Ingleby complains,[38] and like his notorious Alleyn letter. If some one) Tj T*
(only would follow Mr Collier through all his work--pending his hoped-for) Tj T*
(Retractations,--and assure us that the two pieces above-named, and the) Tj T*
(Perkins Folio, are the only things we need reject, such some-one would) Tj T*
(render a great service to all literary antiquarians, and enable them to) Tj T*
(do justice to the wonderful diligence, knowledge, and acumen, of the) Tj T*
(veteran pioneer in their path. Certainly, in most of the small finds) Tj T*
(which we workers at this Text thought we had made, we afterwards found) Tj T*
(we had been anticipated by Mr Collier's _Registers of the Stationers') Tj T*
(Company_, or _Bibliographical Catalogue_, and that the facts were there) Tj T*
(rightly stated. [Header: PRINT THE STATIONERS' REGISTERS.] That there) Tj T*
(is pure metal in Mr Collier's work, and a good deal of it, few will) Tj T*
(doubt; but the dross needs refining out. I hope that the first step in) Tj T*
(the process may be the printing of the whole of the Stationers') Tj T*
(Registers from their start to 1700 at least, by the Camden) Tj T*
(Society,--within whose range this work well lies,--or by the new) Tj T*
(Harleian or some other Society. It ought not to be left to the 'Early) Tj T*
(English Text' to do some 20 years hence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(        F. J. FURNIVALL.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(      _29 Nov., 1869._) Tj T*
