(¶ AN ABRAHAM MAN.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(AN Abraham man is he that walketh bare armed, and bare legged, and) Tj T*
(fayneth hym selfe mad, and caryeth a packe of wool, or a stycke with) Tj T*
(baken on it, or such lyke toy, and nameth himselfe poore Tom.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A RUFFELER.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Ruffeler goeth wyth a weapon to seeke seruice, saying he hath bene a) Tj T*
(Seruitor in the wars, and beggeth for his reliefe. But his chiefest) Tj T*
(trade is to robbe poore wayfaring men and market women.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A PRYGMAN.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Prygman goeth with a stycke in hys hand like an idle person. His) Tj T*
(propertye is to steale cloathes of the hedge, which they call storing of) Tj T*
(the Rogeman: or els filtch Poultry, carying them to the Alehouse, whych) Tj T*
(they call the Bowsyng In, & ther syt playing at cardes and dice, tyl) Tj T*
(that is spent which they haue so fylched.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Header: AWDELEY. THE FRATERNITY OF VACABONDES.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A WHIPIACKE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Whypiacke is one, that by coulor of a counterfaite Lisence \(which they) Tj T*
(call a Gybe, and the seales they cal Iarckes\) doth vse to beg lyke a) Tj T*
(Maryner, But hys chiefest trade is to rob Bowthes in a Faire, or to) Tj T*
(pilfer ware fro_m_ staules, which they cal heauing of the Bowth.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A FRATER.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Frater goeth wyth a like Lisence to beg for some Spittlehouse or) Tj T*
(Hospital. Their pray is co_m_monly vpo_n_ *[leaf 2b.]* poore women as) Tj T*
(they go and come to the Markets.) Tj T*
