(¶ A QUIRE BIRD.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Quire bird is one that came lately out of prison, & goeth to seeke) Tj T*
(seruice. He is co_m_monly a stealer of Horses, which they terme a) Tj T*
(Priggar of Paulfreys.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ AN VPRIGHT MAN.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An Vpright man is one that goeth wyth the trunchion of a staffe, which) Tj T*
(staffe they cal a Filtchma_n_. This man is of so much authority, that) Tj T*
(meeting with any of his profession, he may cal them to accompt, &) Tj T*
(co_m_maund a share or snap vnto him selfe, of al that they haue gained) Tj T*
(by their trade in one moneth. And if he doo them wrong, they haue no) Tj T*
(remedy agaynst hym, no though he beate them, as he vseth co_m_monly to) Tj T*
(do. He may also co_m_maund any of their women, which they cal Doxies, to) Tj T*
(serue his turne. He hath y_e_ chiefe place at any market walke, & other) Tj T*
(assembles, & is not of any to be co_n_troled.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A CURTALL.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Curtall is much like to the Vpright man, but hys authority is not) Tj T*
(fully so great. He vseth commonly to go with a short cloke, like to grey) Tj T*
(Friers, & his woman with him in like liuery, which he calleth his Altham) Tj T*
(if she be hys wyfe, & if she be his harlot, she is called hys Doxy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A PALLIARD.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Palliard is he that goeth in a patched cloke, and hys Doxy goeth in) Tj T*
(like apparell.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ AN IRISHE TOYLE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An Irishe toyle is he that carieth his ware in hys wallet, as laces,) Tj T*
(pins, poyntes, and such like. He vseth to shew no wares vntill he haue) Tj T*
(his almes. And if the good man and wyfe be not in the way, he procureth) Tj T*
(of the ch[i]lldre_n_ or seruants a fleece of wool, or the worth of) Tj T*
(xij.d. of some other thing, for a peniworth of his wares.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(*[leaf 3]* ¶ A IACK MAN.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Iackeman is he that can write and reade, and somtime speake latin. He) Tj T*
(vseth to make counterfaite licences which they call Gybes, and sets to) Tj T*
(Seales, in their language called Iarkes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
