() Tj T*
(¶ A CURTESY MAN.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Curtesy man is one that walketh about the back lanes in London in the) Tj T*
(day time, and sometime in the broade streetes in the night season, and) Tj T*
(when he meeteth some handsome yong man clenly apareled, or some other) Tj T*
(honest Citizen, he maketh humble salutatio_n_s and low curtesy, and) Tj T*
(sheweth him that he hath a worde or two to speake with his mastership.) Tj T*
(This child can behaue him selfe manerly, for he wyll desire him that he) Tj T*
(talketh withall, to take the vpper hand, and shew him much reuerence,) Tj T*
(and at last like his familier acquaintaunce will put on his cap, and) Tj T*
(walke syde by syde, and talke on this fashion: Oh syr, you seeme to be a) Tj T*
(man, and one that fauoureth men, and therefore I am the more bolder to) Tj T*
