() Tj T*
(12 PROCTOUR.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Proctour is he, that will tary long, and bring a lye, when his Maister) Tj T*
(sendeth him on his errand. This is a stibber gibber Knaue, that doth) Tj T*
(fayne tales.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(13 COMMITOUR OF TIDINGES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Commitour of Tidings is he, that is ready to bring his Maister Nouels) Tj T*
(and tidinges, whether they be true or false. This is a tale bearer) Tj T*
(knaue, that wyll report words spoken in his Maisters presence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(14 GYLE HATHER.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Gyle Hather is he, that wyll stand by his Maister when he is at dinner,) Tj T*
(and byd him beware that he eate no raw meate, because he would eate it) Tj T*
(himselfe. This is a pickthanke knaue, that would make his Maister *[leaf) Tj T*
(8b.]* beleue that the Cowe is woode.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(15 BAWDE PHISICKE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Bawde Phisicke, is he that is a Cocke, when his Maysters meate is euyll) Tj T*
(dressed, and he challenging him therefore, he wyl say he wyll eate the) Tj T*
(rawest morsel thereof him selfe. This is a sausye knaue, that wyl) Tj T*
(contrary his Mayster alway.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(16 MOUNCH PRESENT.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Mounch present is he that is a great gentleman, for when his Mayster) Tj T*
(sendeth him with a present, he wil take a tast thereof by the waye. This) Tj T*
(is a bold knaue, that sometyme will eate the best and leaue the worst) Tj T*
(for his Mayster.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(17 COLE PROPHET.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cole Prophet is he, that when his Maister sendeth him on his errand, he) Tj T*
(wyl tel his answer therof to his Maister or he depart from hym. This) Tj T*
(tittiuell knaue commonly maketh the worst of the best betwene hys) Tj T*
(Maister and his friende.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(18 CORY FAUELL.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cory fauell is he, that wyl lye in his bed, and cory the bed bordes in) Tj T*
(which hee lyeth in steede of his horse. This slouthfull knaue wyll) Tj T*
(buskill and scratch when he is called in the morning, for any hast.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
