(19 DYNG THRIFT.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dyng thrift is he, that wil make his Maisters horse eate pies and rybs) Tj T*
(of beefe, and drinke ale and wyne. Such false knaues oft tymes, wil sell) Tj T*
(their Maisters meate to their owne profit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(20 ESEN DROPPERS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Esen Droppers bene they, that stand vnder mens wales or windowes, or in) Tj T*
(any other place, to heare the *[leaf 9]* secretes of a mans house. These) Tj T*
(misdeming knaues wyl stand in corners to heare if they be euill spoken) Tj T*
(of, or waite a shrewd turne.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(21 CHOPLOGYKE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Choplogyke, is he that when his mayster rebuketh him of hys fault he) Tj T*
(wyll geue hym .xx. wordes for one, els byd the deuils Pater noster in) Tj T*
(silence. This proude prating knaue wyll maintaine his naughtines when he) Tj T*
(is rebuked for them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(22 VNTHRIFTE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Vnthrift, is he that wil not put his wearing clothes to washing, nor) Tj T*
(black his owne shoes, nor amend his his \(_sic_\) own wearing clothes.) Tj T*
(This rechles knaue wyl alway be lousy: and say that hee hath no more) Tj T*
(shift of clothes, and slaunder his Maister.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(23 VNGRACIOUS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Vngracious, is he _tha_t by his own will, will heare no maner of) Tj T*
(seruice, without he be compelled therunto by his rulers. This Knaue wil) Tj T*
(sit at the alehouse drinking or playing at dice, or at other games at) Tj T*
(seruice tyme.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(24 NUNQUAM.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Nunquam, is he that when his Maister sendeth him on his errand he wil) Tj T*
(not come againe of an hour or two where he might haue done it in halfe) Tj T*
(an houre or lesse. This knaue will go about his owne errand or pastime) Tj T*
(and saith he cannot speede at the first.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(25 INGRATUS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Ingratus, is he that when one doth all that he can for him, he will) Tj T*
(scant geue him a good report for his labour. This knaue is so ingrate or) Tj T*
(vnkind, _tha_t he considreth not his frend fro_m_ his fo, & wil requit) Tj T*
(euil for good & being put most in trust, wil sonest deceiue his maister.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_FINIS._) Tj T*
