(3, back]* prepared for them a great and a large barne, and a great fat) Tj T*
(oxe sod out in Furmenty for them, with bread _and_ drinke aboundantly to) Tj T*
(furnesh out the premisses; and euery person had two pence, for such was) Tj T*
(the dole. When Night approched, _th_e pore housholders repaired home to) Tj T*
(their houses: the other wayfaring bold beggers remained alnight in _th_e) Tj T*
(barne; and the same barne being serched with light in the night by this) Tj T*
(old man \(and then yonge\), with[49] others, they tolde seuen score) Tj T*
(persons of men, euery of them hauing his woma_n_, except it were two) Tj T*
(wemen that lay alone to gether for some especyall cause. Thus hauing) Tj T*
(their makes to make mery withall, the buriall was turned to bousing) Tj T*
(_and_ belly chere, morning to myrth, fasting to feasting, prayer to) Tj T*
(pastyme _and_ pressing of papes, and lamenting to Lechery. So that it) Tj T*
(may apere this vncomly company hath had a long continuance, but then) Tj T*
(nothinge geuen so much to pylferinge, pyckinge, and spoyling; and, as) Tj T*
