(named here after, our Chyldren wyll muche meruell what kynd of people) Tj T*
(they were: and so, I trust, shal shortly happen of these. For what) Tj T*
(thinge doth chiefely cause these rowsey rakehelles thus to continue and) Tj T*
(dayly increase? Surely a number of wicked parsons that kéepe typlinge) Tj T*
(Houses in all shires, where they haue succour and reliefe; and what so) Tj T*
(euer they bring, they are sure to receaue money for *[leaf 4]* the same,) Tj T*
(for they sell good penyworthes. The byers haue _th_e greatest gayne;) Tj T*
(yea, yf they haue nether money nor ware, they wylbe trusted; their) Tj T*
