(man, and taketh holde of his horse brydell, and leadeth him in to the) Tj T*
(wode, and demaundeth of him what and how much money he had in his purse.) Tj T*
("Now, by my troth," quoth this old man; "you are a merrye gentle man. I) Tj T*
(knowe you meane not to take a waye anye thinge from me, but rather to) Tj T*
(geue me some if I shoulde aske it of you." By and by, this seruant) Tj T*
(thiefe casteth the cloke that he caried on his arme about this poore) Tj T*
(mans face, that he should not marke or vew them, with sharpe words to) Tj T*
(delyuer quicly that he had, and to confesse truly what was in his purse.) Tj T*
