(iust seuen shyllinges in his purse; and the trouth is he knew of no) Tj T*
(more. This old angell was falen out of a lytle purse into the botome of) Tj T*
(a great purse. Now, this seuen shyllings in whyte money they quickly) Tj T*
(founde, thinkinge in dede that there had bene no more; yet farther) Tj T*
(groping and searchinge, found this old angell. And with great) Tj T*
(admiration, this gentleman thyefe begane to blesse hym, sayinge, "good) Tj T*
