(¶ A VPRIGHT MAN. Ca. 2.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(*[leaf 7]* A Vpright[59] man, the second in secte of this vnsemely) Tj T*
(sorte, must be next placed, of these rainginge rablement of rascales;) Tj T*
(some be seruing men, artificers, and laboryng men traded vp in) Tj T*
(husbandry. These not mindinge to get their lyuinge with the swete of) Tj T*
(their face, but casting of all payne, wyll wander, after their wycked) Tj T*
(maner, through the most shyres of this realm,--) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  {As Sommerset shyre, Wylshire, Barke shyre, Oxforde shyre,) Tj T*
(  {Harfordeshyre, Myddilsex, Essex, Suffolke, Northfolke, Sussex,) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Surrye, and Kent, as the cheyfe and best shyres of reliefe. Yea, not) Tj T*
(with out punishment by stockes, whyppinges, and imprisonment, in most of) Tj T*
(these places aboue sayde. Yet, not with standinge they haue so good) Tj T*
(lykinge in their lewed, lecherous loyteringe, that full quiclye all) Tj T*
(their punishmentes is[60] for gotten. And repentaunce is neuer thought) Tj T*
(vpon vntyll they clyme thrée tres with a ladder. These vnrewly rascales,) Tj T*
(in their roylynge, disperse them selues into seuerall companyes, as) Tj T*
(occation serueth, sometyme more and somtyme lesse. As, if they repayre) Tj T*
(to a poore husbandmans house, hée wyll go a lone, or one with him, and) Tj T*
(stoutely demaund his charytie, eyther shewing how he hath serued in the) Tj T*
(warres, and their maymed, eyther that he sekethe seruice, and saythe) Tj T*
(that he woulde be glad to take payne for hys lyuinge, althoughe he) Tj T*
