([Header: HARMAN. A HOKER, OR ANGGLEAR.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A HOKER, OR ANGGLEAR. Cap. 3.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THese hokers, or Angglers, be peryllous and most wicked knaues, and be) Tj T*
(deryued or procede forth from the vpright men; they commenly go in frese) Tj T*
(ierkynes and gally slopes, poynted benethe the kne; these when they) Tj T*
(practise there pylfringe, it is all by night; for, as they walke a day) Tj T*
(times from house to house, to demaund charite, they vigelantly marke) Tj T*
(where or in what place they maye attayne to there praye, casting there) Tj T*
(eyes vp to euery wyndow, well noting what they se their, whether) Tj T*
(apparell or linnen, hanginge nere vnto the sayde wyndowes, and that wyll) Tj T*
(they be sure to haue _th_e next night folowing; [Header: HARMAN. A) Tj T*
(HOKER. A ROGE.] for they customably carry with them a staffe of v. or) Tj T*
(vi. foote long, in which, within one ynch of _th_e tope therof, ys a) Tj T*
(lytle hole bored through, *[leaf 9]* in which hole they putte an yron) Tj T*
(hoke, and with the same they wyll pluck vnto them quickly any thing) Tj T*
(_tha_t they may reche ther with, which hoke in the day tyme they) Tj T*
(couertly cary about them, and is neuer sene or taken out till they come) Tj T*
(to the place where they worke there fete: such haue I sene at my house,) Tj T*
(and haue oft talked with them and haue handled ther staues, not then) Tj T*
(vnderstanding to what vse or inte_n_t they serued, although I hadde and) Tj T*
(perceiued, by there talke and behauiour, great lykelyhode of euyll) Tj T*
(suspition in them: they wyl ether leane vppon there staffe, to hyde the) Tj T*
(hole thereof, when they talke with you, or holde their hande vpon the) Tj T*
(hole; and what stuffe, either wollen or lynnen, they thus hoke out, they) Tj T*
(neuer carye the same forth with to their staulyng kens, but hides the) Tj T*
(same a iij. daies in some secret corner, _and_ after conuayes the same) Tj T*
(to their houses abouesaid, where their host or hostys geueth them money) Tj T*
(for the same, but halfe the value that it is worth, or els their doxes) Tj T*
(shall a farre of sell the same at the like houses. I was credebly) Tj T*
