([Header: HARMAN. A PRYGGE.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(¶ A DRONKEN TINCKAR. Cap. 13.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THese dronken Tynckers, called also Prygges, be beastly people, _and_) Tj T*
(these yong knaues be _th_e wurst. These neuer go w_i_t_h_ out their) Tj T*
(Doxes, and yf their women haue anye thing about them, as apparell or) Tj T*
(lynnen, that is worth the selling, they laye the same to gage, or sell) Tj T*
(it out right, for bene bowse at their bowsing ken. And full sone wyll) Tj T*
(they bée wearye of them, and haue a newe. When they happen one woorke at) Tj T*
(any good house, their Doxes lynger alofe, and tarry for them in some) Tj T*
(corner; and yf he taryeth longe from her, then she knoweth *[leaf 18]*) Tj T*
(he hath worke, and walketh neare, and sitteth downe by him. For besydes) Tj T*
(money, he looketh for meate and drinke for doinge his dame pleasure. For) Tj T*
(yf she haue thrée or foure holes in a pan, hee wyll make as many more) Tj T*
(for spedy gaine. And if he se any old ketle, chafer, or pewter dish) Tj T*
(abroad in the yard where he worketh, hée quicklye snappeth the same vp,) Tj T*
(and in to the booget it goeth round. Thus they lyue with deceite.) Tj T*
