(¶ The vpright Cofe canteth to the Roge.[165]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(*The vpright man speaketh to the Roge.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VPRIGHTMAN.[166]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Bene Lightmans to thy quarromes, in what lipken hast thou lypped in) Tj T*
(    this darkemans, whether in a lybbege or in the strummell?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    *God morrowe to thy body, in what house hast thou lyne in all night,) Tj T*
(    whether in a bed, or in the strawe?*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ROGE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    I couched a hogshead in a Skypper this darkemans.) Tj T*
