() Tj T*
(VPRIGHT MAN.[168]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    I towre the strummel trine vpon thy nabchet[169] _and_ Togman.) Tj T*
(    *I sée the strawe hang vpon thy cap and coate.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ROGE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    I saye by the Salomon I will lage it of with a gage of benebouse;) Tj T*
(    then cut to my nose watch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    *I sweare by the masse[170], I wull washe it of with a quart of good) Tj T*
(    drynke; [leaf 29][171] then saye to me what thou wylt.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    MAN. Why, hast thou any lowre in thy bonge to bouse?) Tj T*
(         *Why, hast thou any money in thy purse to drinke?*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    ROGE. But a flagge, a wyn, and a make.) Tj T*
(          *But a grot, a penny, and a halfe penny.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    MAN. Why, where is the kene that hath the bene bouse?) Tj T*
(         *where is the house that hath good drinke?*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    ROGE. A bene mort hereby at the signe of the prauncer.) Tj T*
(          *A good wyfe here by at the signe of the hors.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    MAN. I cutt it is quyer buose, I bousd a flagge the laste dark mans.) Tj T*
(         *I saye it is small and naughtye drynke. I dranke a groate there) Tj T*
(         the last night.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    ROGE. But bouse there a bord, _and_ thou shalt haue beneship.) Tj T*
(          *But drinke there a shyllinge, and thou shalt haue very good.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Tower ye yander is the kene, dup the gygger, and maund that is bene) Tj T*
(    shyp.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    *Se you, yonder is the house, open the doore, and aske for the best.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    MAN. This bouse is as benshyp[172] as rome bouse.) Tj T*
(         *This drinke is as good as wyne.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Now I tower that bene bouse makes nase nabes.) Tj T*
(    *Now I se that good drinke makes a dronken heade.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Maunde of this morte what bene pecke is in her ken.) Tj T*
(    *Aske of this wyfe what good meate shee hath in her house.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    ROGE. She hath a Cacling chete, a grunting chete, ruff Pecke, cassan,) Tj T*
(          and popplarr of yarum.) Tj T*
(          *She hath a hen, a pyg, baken, chese and mylke porrage.*) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    MAN. That is beneshyp to our watche.) Tj T*
ET
