(seeming to giue him some money, and with fayre allusions brought him) Tj T*
(into the stréete, where he charged the constable with him, affirminge) Tj T*
(him to be the counterfet Cranke that ranne away vpon Alholon daye last.) Tj T*
(The constable being very loth to medle with him, but the printer knowing) Tj T*
(him and his depe disceit, desyred he mought be brought before the) Tj T*
(debutie of the ward, which straight was accomplished, which whe_n_ he) Tj T*
(came before the debuty, he demaunded of him of whence he was and what) Tj T*
(was his name; he answered as before he did vnto _th_e printer: the) Tj T*
(debutie asked the printer what he woulde laye vnto hys charge; he) Tj T*
(answered and aleged him to be a vagabond and depe deceyuer of the) Tj T*
(people, and the counterfet Crank that ran away vpon Alhallon day last) Tj T*
(from the constable of Newington and him, and requested him earnestly to) Tj T*
(send him to ward: the debuty thinking him to be deceiued, but) Tj T*
(neuerthelesse laid his co_m_maundement vpon him, so that the printer) Tj T*
(should beare his charges if he could not iustifie it; he agréed) Tj T*
(thereunto. And so he and the constable went to cary him to the Counter:) Tj T*
(and as they were going vnder Ludgate, this crafty Cranke toke his héeles) Tj T*
(and ran down the hill as fast as he could dryve, the constable and the) Tj T*
(printer after him as fast as they coulde; but the printer of _th_e twayn) Tj T*
(being lighter of fote, ouertoke him at fleete bridge, and with strong) Tj T*
(hand caried him to the counter, and safely deliuered him. In _th_e morow) Tj T*
(_th_e printer sent his boy that stripped him vpon Alhalon day at night) Tj T*
(to view him, because he would be sure, which boy knew him very well:) Tj T*
(this Crank confessed unto the debuty, _tha_t he had hosted the night) Tj T*
(before in Kent stréet in Southwarke, at the sign of the Cock, which) Tj T*
(thing to be true, the printer sente to know, and found him a lyer; but) Tj T*
(further inquiring, at length found out his habitation, dwelling in) Tj T*
(maister Hilles rentes, hauinge a pretye house, well stuffed, with a) Tj T*
(fayre ioyne table, and a fayre cubbard garnished with peuter, hauing an) Tj T*
(old auncient woman to his wyfe. The printer being sure therof, repaired) Tj T*
(vnto the Counter, and rebuked him for his beastly behaviour, and told) Tj T*
(him of his false fayning, willed him to confesse it, and aske) Tj T*
(forgivenes: he perceyued him to know his depe dissimulation, relented,) Tj T*
(and confessed all his disceit; and so remayning in the counter thrée) Tj T*
(dayes, was removed to Brydwel, where he was strypt starke naked, and his) Tj T*
(ougly attyre put vpo_n_ him before the maisters thereof, who wondered) Tj T*
(greatly at his dissimulation: for which offence he stode vpon the) Tj T*
(pillery in Cheapsyde, both in his ougly and handsome attyre. And after) Tj T*
(that went in the myll whyle his ougly picture was a drawing; and then) Tj T*
