(A SHIFTER.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Shifter, not long since, going ordinarily booted, got leaue of a) Tj T*
(Carrier to ride on his owne hackney a little way from London, who,) Tj T*
(comming to the Inne where the Carier that night should lodge, honestly) Tj T*
(set vp the horse, and entred the hal, where were at one table some three) Tj T*
(and thirty clothiers, all returning to their seuerall countries. Vsing,) Tj T*
(as he could, his curtesie, and being Gentleman-like attirde, he was at) Tj T*
(all their instance placed at the vpper end by the hostesse. After hee) Tj T*
(had a while eaten, he fel to discourse with such pleasance, that all the) Tj T*
(table were greatly delighted therewith. In the midst of supper enters a) Tj T*
(noise of musitions, who with their instruments added a double delight.) Tj T*
(For them hee requested his hostesse to laye a shoulder of mutton and a) Tj T*
(couple of capons to the fire, for which he would pay, _and_ then mooued) Tj T*
(in their behalfe to gather. Among them a noble was made, which he) Tj T*
(fingring, was well blest; for before he had not a crosse, yet he promist) Tj T*
(to make it vp an angel. To be short, in comes the reckoning, which \(by) Tj T*
(reason of the fine fare _and_ excesse of wine\) amounted to each mans) Tj T*
(halfe crown. Then hee requested his hostesse to prouide so many possets) Tj T*
(of sacke, as would furnish the table, which he would bestow on the) Tj T*
(Gentlemen to requite their extraordinary costs: _and_ iestingly askt if) Tj T*
(she would make him her deputie to gather the reckoning; she graunted,) Tj T*
(and he did so: and on a sodaine, \(faining to hasten his hostesse with) Tj T*
(the possets\) he tooke his cloke, and, finding fit time, hee slipt out of) Tj T*
(doores, leauing the guestes and their hostesse to a new reckoning, _and_) Tj T*
(the musitians to a good supper, but they paid for the sauce. This iest) Tj T*
(some vntruly attribute to a man of excellent parts about London, but he) Tj T*
(is slandered: the party that performed it hath scarce any good qualitie) Tj T*
(to liue. Of these sort I could set downe a great number, but I leaue you) Tj T*
(now vnto those which by Maister Harman are discouered.) Tj T*
